inline_comments.body:
Follow-up: the consequence is broader than the offload case. This validation runs inside `Scheduler.schedule()` (`build_connector_meta`), so each of the following propagates out of the engine step and kills EngineCore (`core.py:1508`):
- the `ValueError` here;
- a `KeyError` when the manifest has no `block_size` or `keys`;
- an `IndexError` when `keys` is shorter than `start // block_size + 1`.

`aux_output_prefix` comes from client-supplied `kv_transfer_params`, so one malformed request fails every in-flight request. Please validate the manifest when the request is admitted (input processing or `add_request`), and reject only that request.
